    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Hello, I am Youngjae Woo, a computational biologist based in San Diego specializing in the intersection of human genetics and artificial intelligence. My research leverages large-scale biomedical datasets to identify novel therapeutic targets and elucidate their underlying biological mechanisms. By translating complex, high-dimensional genomic data into clear, actionable insights, I aim to bridge the gap between frontier computational methodology and tangible clinical breakthroughs.</p>
    <p>Currently, my work is focused on applying advanced deep learning architectures—including models like Geneformer and ChromBPNet—to both target discovery and downstream drug development. Beyond my direct research, I am actively involved in fostering the local and global biotech community, advising industry associations, and facilitating knowledge exchange on the latest AI tools among bio-pharma professionals. Ultimately, I am deeply passionate about driving therapeutic innovation and translating data-driven science into clinical practice.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/youngjaewoo">Find me on GitHub →</a></p>
